<<~ ahu #/bearing>>
! Example Zero — Olympos / Gigantomachy

A complete art-direction *example* rather than a commissioned render, fixed geographic map, or independent source of Elyncian canon. Its illustrative assignment: an in-house concept-art board depicting exploratory **artworks about Olympos**, not a portrait of the people who make or view the board. The addressed audience may include cartographers and game artists. Artists, directors, critics, photographers, and viewers remain outside the depicted scene unless the specific work explicitly includes them. Tiny travelers can inhabit an **inner** illustration of the Marches.

Outer subject: a physically assembled wall/pinboard of paintings, maps, charcoal drawings, overlays, working alternatives, media tests and revisions. Inner subjects: mountain panoramas, the Rift passage, the Phlegra wounds, artifacts, refuges, hazards, and travel studies. Some inner images challenge others through visible correction rather than decorative overlap.
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/settled-world>>
!! Preserved Elyncian bearings

* Shattered Heights of Olympos, Rift of Tempes and Ash Plains of Phlegra occupy the Olympian Marches.
* Marches connect Neo-Thracia and Illyria and approach the Aegean Nexus of New Delos.
* Millennia of Gigantomachy electromagnetic, magitech and sorcerous contamination precede roughly five centuries of maelstrom enclosure.
* Following the maelstrom enclosure, the reopened corridor admits hazardous passage and pockets of survival.
* Illyria's Necrospire impact lies in the Accursed Mountains, **not** on Olympos.
* Exact route geometry, relic identity, settlements, supernatural mechanisms and boundaries remain open. The Gorgonne Diaspora counts among the established named regional powers, but no specific settlement or encounter follows automatically.
* Olympos serves exploratory visual/terrain inquiry; Neo-Thracia's watershed retains precedence as the first approved game-worthy atlas project.
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/artist-register>>
!! Named artistic ancestors and their contributions

* **Tom Patterson** — shaded relief, mountain/seafloor coherence, colour and detail generalization.
* **Bernhard Jenny** — plan oblique, relief geometry, Swiss colour shading and aerial perspective.
* **Heinrich Berann** — panoramic landform orchestration from summit toward lowland and sea.
* **Eduard Imhof** — tonal hierarchy, illumination, calm depth in complexity.
* **Erwin Raisz** — memorable physiographic forms and purposeful terrain simplification.
* **Jean Giraud / Moebius** — luminous air, economical line, vast silent science-fantasy spaces.
* **Luka Rejec** — mythpunk travel, strange relics, gameable exploratory geography.
* **Giovanni Battista Piranesi** — architectural immensity and ruined engineering.
* **Ian Miller** — corroded organic-mechanical density within isolated scars.
* **Kilian Eng** — localized psychedelic/retro-futurist anomalous illumination.
* **Gustave Doré** — sublimity, chiaroscuro and small figures against immense landscapes.

Influences concern craft techniques and viewer effects; do not reproduce specific identifiable artworks or print the artist registry on the board.
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/story>>
!! Narrative relationship, depiction scopes, and visual argument

**Audience/address:** a collaborator reviewing hypotheses about a setting. **Artifactual narrative:** a collection of studies accumulated across differing questions and opinions. **Subject narrative:** a sacred mountain badly wounded by ancient war, later smothered by maelstrom, now difficult but possible to traverse. Audience and hypothetical makers stay *outside* the image.

Primary first read: a sweeping high, luminous relief-aware Olympos panorama. Second read: a damaged passage and dark Phlegra/relic studies with substantially heavier line and contrast. Later read: a route overlay visibly disputes the panorama, a charcoal alternative questions a giant-bone interpretation, and a modest refuge challenges the idea of universal uninhabitability.

Difference of opinion need not become explanatory text. Two mismatched drainage traces, an erased crossing, a stained scrap with revised colour, and a partly concealed earlier silhouette can communicate revision through their juxtaposition. Papers overlap because the artists compare something specific.
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/source-invocations>>
!! Complete semantic-call sequence (native procedure names; definitions live in companion procedures meme)

The following calls carry the example as modular black ink. A standalone authoring tiddler imports the companion native procedure definitions before these calls. This source describes an artwork; it does not invoke image generation.

```tiddlywiki
<<art-work name:"ELYNCIA — OLYMPOS / GIGANTOMACHY" kind:"physical in-house environment concept-art pinboard" purpose:"compare unresolved terrain, artifact, route and hazard interpretations in the Olympian Marches">>
<<art-address audience:"cartographers, environment artists and art directors" relationship:"outside the depicted studio; review the pictured studies as evidence" invitation:"compare, question and revise without assuming the place has already been mapped">>
<<art-depict subject:"an irregular pinboard holding different handmade images" setting:"physical working surface with clipped-off sheets, pins, tape, vellum overlays and selective handwritten marks" location:"outer artifact only; all traveler figures appear inside the mountain studies, never as studio observers">>
<<art-read first:"luminous coherent Olympos panorama" second:"dark mythpunk relic and Phlegra studies with one difficult crossing" third:"conflicting route sketches, alternate relic interpretations, a sheltering refuge, and distinct paper histories">>

<<art-reference artist:"Tom Patterson" contribution:"clear physiographic relief" application:"connected summits, drainage, lowlands and distant shore">>
<<art-reference artist:"Bernhard Jenny" contribution:"plan-oblique landform profile and aerial perspective" application:"panoramic mountain geometry and selective elevation contrast">>
<<art-reference artist:"Heinrich Berann" contribution:"painted continuous panorama" application:"summit-to-Aegean spatial sweep">>
<<art-reference artist:"Eduard Imhof and Erwin Raisz" contribution:"tonal relief hierarchy and characteristic landform language" application:"quiet distant hills and legible ridgeline shapes">>
<<art-reference artist:"Jean Giraud / Moebius" contribution:"negative space and fine science-fantasy contours" application:"clear high atmosphere, small travelers, open calm passages">>
<<art-reference artist:"Luka Rejec" contribution:"mythpunk exploration and strange archaeology" application:"traversable but hazardous route and unsettling discoveries">>
<<art-reference artist:"Piranesi, Ian Miller, Kilian Eng, Gustave Doré" contribution:"ruinous immensity, localized corrosive linework, anomalous luminosity, sacred scale" application:"dark lower-right Phlegra and relic studies contrasted with pale high country">>

<<art-view system:"partly plan-oblique painterly panorama" spatial-rule:"physiographically coherent ridges, ravines, passes, basins and drainage descending toward lower country" limits:"not a surveyed georeferenced route map; inset relation maps may use different spatial conventions">>
<<art-contrast left:"clear upper mountain painting" right:"dark lower-right war scar studies" relation:"maintain distinct regional style weather within a shared imagined landscape">>
<<art-place element:"panorama" site:"large, dominant, off-centre sheet" action:"one translucent route overlay intersects a specific disputed valley">>
<<art-place element:"relic sketch" site:"cropped at lower-right edge" action:"dark charcoal silhouette partly covers a lighter incompatible bone hypothesis">>
<<art-place element:"small habitat vignette" site:"lower-left warm island" action:"a quiet spring and terraces contest total-wasteland interpretation">>

<<art-study question:"Where does the Rift route actually pass?" form:"graphite over translucent vellum" proposal:"an amended crossing follows a gentler saddle rather than the panoramic artist's impossible escarpment" status:"unresolved; two visible route lines">>
<<art-dispute study-a:"hero panorama" study-b:"transparent route overlay" disagreement:"route and drainage disagree at one saddle" visible-proof:"erased pass mark beneath the translucent corrected line">>
<<art-study question:"What lies exposed beneath Phlegra's vitrified layers?" form:"cool-grey charcoal and white chalk" proposal:"bone-like form could indicate giant remains or distorted mechanical/rock strata" status:"two adjacent interpretations; identity withheld">>
<<art-study question:"Which hazards have distinct signatures?" form:"three loose colour experiment scraps" proposal:"cyan static near charged ridges; amber ancient mechanism leakage; violet spatial discontinuities" status:"tentative visual vocabulary">>
<<art-study question:"How can a small community persist?" form:"gouache vignette" proposal:"protected water, terraced stone, reused masonry and repair labor" status:"unnamed speculative refuge">>

<<art-media support:"large warm-white cold-press watercolor sheet" medium:"watercolor and thin opaque gouache" implement:"broad brushes with fine pen accents" technique:"large grouped value masses, limited mountain contour detail" handling:"an unfinished luminous sky zone and one curling edge">>
<<art-media support:"cool charcoal-grey fibrous stock" medium:"charcoal and chalk" implement:"stick and rubbed stump" technique:"broad rubbed darks, sparse sharp white structural marks" handling:"one obvious erased/reworked geological hypothesis">>
<<art-media support:"thin pale blue-grey tracing vellum" medium:"graphite and ink" implement:"technical pen and pencil" technique:"sparse linework over another image" handling:"transparent route correction with underlying marks visible">>
<<art-media support:"smooth neutral white Bristol" medium:"ink and opaque paint" implement:"fine nib and brush" technique:"localized relic sections and decisive material planes" handling:"clean cut, noticeably smoother than charcoal stock">>
<<art-media support:"small cream, cool blue and stained pale ochre scraps" medium:"thin color washes" implement:"small brush" technique:"small experiments of different hazard illumination" handling:"mixed clipped/torn edges and genuinely different paper tones">>

<<art-edge region:"distant Olympos hills and open sky" contour:"soft and occasionally lost" contrast:"lower with aerial recession" detail:"broad, quiet masses without fine surface scratches">>
<<art-edge region:"foreground relic study" contour:"selective crisp damaged edges" contrast:"strong but localized" detail:"distinct bronze patina, mineral strata and large untreated surfaces">>
<<art-withhold region:"high bright sky and far sea" absence:"uniform grain, high-frequency crackle and lettering" purpose:"allow breathing room against the denser Phlegra studies">>
<<art-withhold region:"uncertain skeletal form" absence:"conclusive deity or giant identification" purpose:"preserve competing in-world archaeological interpretations">>

<<art-history layer:"Gigantomachy before enclosure" evidence:"vitrified scars, gigantic debris and persistent strange emissions" interpretation:"multiple ancient mechanisms remain unconfirmed">>
<<art-history layer:"roughly five centuries of maelstrom" evidence:"deposited ash, preserved pockets, changed surfaces, covered infrastructure" interpretation:"later action on a far older war-wounded region">>
<<art-history layer:"reopened present" evidence:"travelers inside a route sketch, maintained crossing, protected refuge" interpretation:"danger remains; human persistence survives">>

<<art-boundary scope:"Elyncian geography" preserve:"Heights of Olympos; Rift of Tempes; Ash Plains of Phlegra; Marches between Neo-Thracia and Illyria and near New Delos Aegean approaches; Necrospire belongs to Illyria's Accursed Mountains" undecided:"exact distances, watershed edits, borders, route geometry, settlement identities">>
<<art-boundary scope:"representation" preserve:"artist/viewer outside image; any humanoids belong to the embedded fictional depictions" undecided:"identity of divine relics and supernatural processes">>
<<art-boundary scope:"presentation" preserve:"real working evidence and regional stylistic contrast" undecided:"which studio conjecture will prevail; do not print artist influences, evaluation settings or revision histories on the board">>
```
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/further-resource-ahu>>
!! Resource and source ahu

* Canon bearings: Elyncia `nexuses/new-delos/region-worksheet.mem`, `nexuses/illyria/region-worksheet.mem`, Neo-Thracia referee worksheet (restricted register), and region-worksheet template in the Synthetic Dream Machine repository. The source files, not this exploration, govern setting claims.
* Tom Patterson and Bernhard Jenny, *Introducing Plan Oblique Relief*: https://cartographicperspectives.org/index.php/journal/article/view/cp57-jenny-patterson
* Getty Research Institute Art & Architecture Thesaurus (AAT): https://www.getty.edu/research/conducting_research/vocabularies/aat/
* Getty Categories for the Description of Works of Art: https://www.getty.edu/publications/categories-description-works-art/categories/ ; Materials/Techniques: https://www.getty.edu/publications/categories-description-works-art/categories/object-architecture-group/7/ ; Subject Matter: https://www.getty.edu/publications/categories-description-works-art/categories/object-architecture-group/16/
* W. J. T. Mitchell, *Picture Theory*: metapictures and pictures-about-pictures.
* Kress and van Leeuwen, *Reading Images*: represented participants vs audiences and composition.
* Michael Baxandall, *Patterns of Intention*: inferred design problems and historically situated choices.
* James Gurney, *Color and Light*: specific relationships among light, material and atmosphere.
* Harvard Project Zero: https://pz.harvard.edu/resources/what-makes-you-say
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/handoff>>
!! Future use

* "New Example Zero, all new themes/details, same cartographers but different artists, talk it out first" — preserve only explicitly locked cartographers; explore subject, address, nested depiction, and creative tensions through dialogue before authoring. Do not carry forward Olympos, the same studies, or fantasy as defaults.
* "Examine this image and reverse engineer its art sigils" — apply `art-sigils-formal-analysis.mem` first; return observable evidence, plausible interpretations, alternative readings and candidate modular calls with uncertainty intact.
* "Fire the sigil" — a distinct image-making request; this example supplies art direction without independently initiating any rendering.
<<~/ahu>>